seg-64581554e84a = <b>Files:</b> the { "120" } product files (GeoJSON, PNG, incident JSON, manifest per day) are <b>not in git</b>. The hash of every file is in <c1/>, and a day can be rebuilt from its archive and compared.

# text
# c1: manifest.json
seg-c89b88dc3d3b = Example of what a day reads: on 2026-09-15 the archive held { "110,619,797" } position rows in { "79,826" } trace files; { "103.0" } million were outside the box, { "5.6" } million were not ADS-B, { "1.2" } million were on the ground or below { "5,000" } ft, { "0.6" } million carried no accuracy field, and { "212,426" } were aggregated (<c1/> input counters).

# text
seg-cc590aa74075 = Three days (2026-09-18, 2026-09-26, 2026-10-03) were fetched again from the archive and run a second time: the GeoJSON, the PNG and the incident file are <b>byte-identical</b> to the first run (SHA-256 equal), so the product is deterministic even though the identifier hash salt is random per run.

