seg-097ed1aa1504 = <c1/>, <c2/> and <c3/> each change the number of degraded cells by a factor of two or more on every day; relaxing <c4/> to { "6" } turns { "1" } degraded cell into { "12" } on 09-26 (Jaccard with the registered set { "0.08" }). On 09-18 raising <c5/> to { "0.4" } keeps { "1" } of the { "8" } (Jaccard { "0.125" }). A cell call near the thresholds is a statement about the thresholds as much as about the data.

# text
# c1: min_aircraft_sampled
seg-0d0c96099d30 = <b><c1/> mostly moves cells between not degraded and not observed</b>: on 09-18 it leaves the degraded count at { "8" } while { "21" } to { "56" } cells change state.

# text
# c1: background_margin
# c2: min_baseline_good_reports
# c3: day_confound_background
seg-04cc05318a5d = <b>Three guards are inactive here</b>: <c1/>, <c2/> and <c3/> change nothing on any of the three days (the background share is { "0" }), so this region and period say nothing about how well they work. They would matter where a regional effect raises the background.

# text
seg-7ba403b84fbd = <b>A coarser grid ({ "1.0" } degree) changes the picture</b> ({ "2" }, { "3" } and { "1" } degraded cells; the published cells fall to about a third, { "226" } against { "694" } on 09-18, because each cell is four times larger): cell size is a method choice, and the observatory fixes it at { "0.5" } degrees.

